% Problem 28. Chace vol. II pl. 51 (photograph XII, register 5), PDF pp. 149-150; Peet pp. 63-64 (Pl. J).
No. 28
"{2/3 is: to be added, '3 is: to be subtracted,} 10 remains."   % Chace fn 1: literally "to go in ... to go out"; the scribe wrote only the determinatives (legs) of two verbs as symbols
"Make '10 of 10 this; there becomes 1; the remainder is: 9."   % Peet fn 1: "The B.M.Facs. has, erroneously, 20" (for the second 10); not a reading of the papyrus
"2/3 of it, namely 6, is: to be added to it; the total is 15. '3 of it is: 5. Lo 5 is what went out; the remainder is: 10."
"The doing as it occurs."   % Chace fn 4: "The scribe has omitted the proof here and the statement of the next problem"; Peet: "There has been a considerable error in copying at this point"
% the sums in the words (10 less 1 is 9; 9 and 6 are 15; 15 less 5 is 10) are written as sentences, not as statements, since the papyrus sets out no working for them
